NAME
       echo - print arguments

SYNOPSIS
       echo [-neE] [string ...]

DESCRIPTION
       Writes its arguments separated by single spaces, followed by a
       newline.

OPTIONS
       -n     do not print the trailing newline
       -e     interpret backslash escapes in the arguments
       -E     do not interpret backslash escapes (default)
       --help show a short help text

NOTES
       csh(1) delegates its builtin echo to this program, so scripts
       and the shell behave the same way.

SEE ALSO
       printf(1), csh(1)
